# DONNER tests and visual QA

`npm test` is ~400 fast `node:test` cases. It does **not** compare screenshots.

## Screenshots

Do **not** take Chrome/headless screenshots, write `.tmp-qa/*.png`, or `Read` PNGs into chat after a CSS/HTML/JS tweak.

Screenshot **only** when the human asked, or the bug *is* layout (overlap, clip, wrong sheet, canvas blank). Then:

- One viewport unless phone vs desktop is the bug
- `--virtual-time-budget` ≤ 4000 ms
- Do **not** `Read` the PNG into the model. Say pass/fail in text. Leave files in `.tmp-qa/` (gitignored).

`npm test` plus the changed files is enough for logic, IA, and known CSS regressions.

## Layout tests (`test/gui-css.test.js`, `test/ia.test.js`)

Lock **IDs, order, existence, show/hide**. Do **not** add pixel CSS (`min-width`, `padding`, `font-size`, colors, `z-index`, `calc(…px)`).

Keep the few phone-blank-canvas regressions (`#view` no `transform`, inset+100%, overlay containing block, iOS `pointer-events`).

